{
  "clause": "S290",
  "about": "AirPlay row, master and stored own volume. k = (zone/100)(master/100); level D = min(100, own x k); the row shows D rounded down with 0.01 of slack. Ops, applied in order to one speaker that starts at own 0: own sets the own volume; stored_own is one loaded from settings, a preset or an add, kept unclamped above and at least 0; row_move moves the row to R (sends D = R and stores own = R / k); step is a remote VolumeUp (+5) or VolumeDown (-5), a row move to the shown row plus the step, clamped to 0 to 100; tv_level is a level read back from the speaker and device_volume a DACP DeviceVolume, both a change made on the speaker (D = value, own = D / k); master moves the master and keeps own. sent false marks a step that sends nothing and changes nothing (k at 0, an up step at 100, a down step at 0). After each step, level is the D the speaker has, own_after the stored own volume (both within 1e-6) and row what the row shows.",
